.TH FL-EDIT 1 "November 2026" "fldesktop 0.1.0" "fldesktop"
.SH NAME
fl-edit \- text editor
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBfl-edit\fR [\fIFILE\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
A tabbed text editor with find and replace (Ctrl+F, Ctrl+H, F3), go to line (Ctrl+G), auto-indent,
block indent with Tab/Shift+Tab, word wrap and line numbers.
.SS Syntax highlighting
The language is detected from the file name or the first line (\fB#!\fR interpreter,
\fB<?php\fR, \fB<!DOCTYPE html>\fR, \fBdiff\fR headers). Supported: C/C++, C#, CMake, CSS, Diff, Go,
HTML (with embedded JavaScript and CSS), INI, Java, JavaScript, JSON, Kotlin, Lua, Makefile, Markdown,
Meson, Perl, PHP, Python, Ruby, Rust, Shell, SQL, TOML, TypeScript, XML and YAML.
\fBView \(-> Language\fR overrides the detection for the current tab.
.PP
\fBView \(-> Color Theme\fR picks the highlighting colors: Automatic (follows the desktop's light or
dark theme), Default Light, Default Dark, Solarized Light, Solarized Dark, Monokai or High Contrast.
\fBView \(-> Highlight Matching Brackets\fR marks the bracket next to the cursor and its partner;
brackets inside strings and comments are ignored.
.SH FILES
.TP
\fI~/.config/fldesktop/edit.ini\fR
Settings: \fBColorTheme\fR, \fBMatchBrackets\fR, \fBHighlight\fR, \fBFontSize\fR, \fBTabWidth\fR and others.
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBfl-wm\fR(1), \fBfl-session\fR(1), \fBfl-panel\fR(1)
